# Allowlist for scripts/pclaude-check.sh. It lists text the check would flag
# in skills/pclaude/ but that is meant to be there.
#
# One entry per line:
#   <path glob, relative to skills/pclaude/><TAB><exact text on the flagged line>
# A hit is allowed only when the text it matched lies inside an occurrence of
# that exact text, on a line of a file the glob matches. `*` matches within a
# path segment and `**/` matches any number of directories.
#
# Every entry must sit in a block that opens with a `#` comment saying why it
# is allowed. A blank line ends a block. An entry without a comment fails the
# check, and an entry that no longer matches anything is printed as a warning
# so it can be deleted.

# The footer spec section 4 puts on every SKILL.md credits upstream by name.
**/SKILL.md	Ported from pstack by poteto (MIT). See skills/pclaude/LICENSE.
